\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Overview. A public score matrix, an investment model (independent non-negative per-task gains with L1 or L0 cost), and an aggregation rule define an instance in which a target model must become strictly first. A planner proposes a gain plan; a trusted verifier recomputes the rule on the modified matrix; efficiency is the cost of the evaluator's reference plan divided by the cost of the verified plan, capped at 2.}}{2}{figure.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{2}{Overview. A public score matrix, an investment model (independent non-negative per-task gains with L1 or L0 cost), and an aggregation rule define an instance in which a target model must become strictly first. A planner proposes a gain plan; a trusted verifier recomputes the rule on the modified matrix; efficiency is the cost of the evaluator's reference plan divided by the cost of the verified plan, capped at 2}{figure.caption.3}{}}
